        {
          "label": "Time Difference Per Day",
          "unit": "microseconds",
          "formula": "(1 - TDF) × 86400000000"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Einstein's general relativity predicts that time flows slower in stronger gravitational fields. This effect has been measured with atomic clocks at different altitudes. Near massive objects like neutron stars or black holes, this effect becomes dramatic.",
      "relatedMovies": ["Interstellar", "Arrival"],
      "formula": "Δt = t₀√(1 - 2GM/c²r)"
    },
